# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined tp4/window-next four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/window-next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# The ABAB block of the round-host levers, LEAN: H2 (A), H3 (B), H4 (A), H5 (B) run the SAME six tests (warmup, one coding stream, concurrent4_steady, concurrent8_steady, eight 4k code users, eight 32k code users), so the
# first pair is the exactness read (the round-host pack's E1/E2) and all four are the timing (its T1-T4, eight live: the steady and 32k windows; the 128k window and the four-live pairs T5-T8 are not in this lean path). The
# control for every pair is c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost-log (the Lever N traffic profile plus the ledger flag and nothing else) and the arm is c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost (the control plus SELECT, READ, KEYED and LEAN). H5 (B, SECOND): H3 again, after its own reset. READ the pairs H2/H3 and H4/H5, PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians, INSIDE each length's mean-position window (steady below 8,192; 32k 28,672 to 40,960; 100
# matched rounds a window else VOID; the load rule applied): python3 scripts/ci/w2ln_timing_compare.py pair <A> <B> --live 8 --window <steady|32k> ... and the floor from the two A runs, then the attribution,
# python3 scripts/ci/round_host_report.py pair <A> <B> --live 8 (the host time of every phase of the step, B minus A). GO at a length: both pairs measured and negative and the pooled median gain above the A-to-A floor
# (the estimate, from the integration image's real logs, is about -4.5 ms of a 157 ms eight-live round). NO-GO: a pair positive by more than the floor, a text difference, a stall. A VOID pair is no vote.
# Duration (estimate): 55 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code_32k
